{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1537346-garou-pre-first-change","id":1537346,"title":"Garou Pre-First Change","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-06-14T12:06:56-07:00","id":1537346,"title":"Garou Pre-First Change","content":"I just ran a Werewolf game where the players were children, and it raised a lot of questions about what exactly the mechanics are for pre first change Garou.<br /> <br /> I had been running them as kinfolk, but someone told me that this was wrong, that Garou to be are different from the moment of birth.<br /> <br /> A few questions:<br /> <br /> I addition to genetics, there is a &quot;spiritual component&quot; to Garou. When does this spiritual change come about? At conception? At birth? At puberty? At the moment of first change? Pre-ordained by Gaia since the dawn of time? <br /> <br /> Can said spiritual component be detected by supernatural powers? I think 5E says &quot;Scent of the True Form&quot; works, but is this the case in earlier editions? What about other powers?<br /> <br /> Are garou subject to the delirium before their first change?<br /> <br /> Can pre-first change garou purchase Gnosis or Gifts in the manner of Kinfolk?<br /> <br /> If yes, is their Gnosis lowered by having silver equipment?<br /> <br /> Does silver pain or cause aggravated damage to garou pre first change?<br /> <br /> <br /> What happens if a vampire tries to embrace a garou before their first change?<br /> Can a garou awaken as a mage pre first change? What is awakening is forced on them by Alchemy Six or Prime Nine?<br /> Can a garou become a mummy before their first change is subject to the spell of life?<br /> Is there any way a changeling soul can be attached to a garou pre first change?<br /> What would happen if a group pre first change performed the Rite of Sacred Rebirth?<br /> Or, even crazier, what would happen if a pre first change shapeshifter who was kin to multiple breeds performed the Rite of Sacred Rebirth to transform into a different breed than they would have become naturally with their first change?<br /> <br /> <br /> So, we know from the flavor text that most Garou have their first change when they frenzy for the first time after being placed in a stressful situation. But frenzy is typically the result of a certain number of successes on a rage roll, right? But, Garou don't have Rage until their first change, right?<br /> So isn't this something of a catch 22? Is this meant to be purely storyteller FIAT?<br /> This actually came up in my game, the PCs violently kidnapped an adolescent black spiral dancer who had not yet undergone her first change, and I made a rage roll for her to see if she would frenzy and undergo her first change as the result of the stress (she did) and the players told me I was cheating because, by definition, if she hasn't had her first change yet, she has no rage score to roll.<br /> <br /> <br /> And a similar, but unrelated question: Wolves and Coyotes can produce fertile offspring. Is it possible to have coyotes who are garou kinfolk or wolves who are nuwisha kinfolk? Could such kinfolk ever breed true?<br /> <br /> <br /> Thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26576-talakeal","name":"Talakeal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-14T14:01:40-07:00","id":1537356,"title":"","content":"So... the short version? The books don't really support playing pre-Change Garou. Even if W5 decreased the difficulty of this slightly, it's still not meant for it. As such, a huge amount of what you're asking is never really addressed because it doesn't really come up in the intended play of the game.<br /> <br /> As I respond to a few specifics, a big caveat: Editions matter. With five editions of the game, there's a lot of small details that impact things. I'm going to do my best to address things broadly, but my statements will be variable in &quot;truth&quot; if you hold one edition as the primary one over others.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Talakeal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1537346-garou-pre-first-change#post1537346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I had been running them as kinfolk, but someone told me that this was wrong, that Garou to be are different from the moment of birth.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pre-change Garou are not kinfolk mechanically. Telling the difference is not necessarily simple though. Kinfolk are resistant to Delirium in some fashion, and children that are immune to Delrium aren't inherently comfortable around giant murder monsters just because there isn't magic forcing them to act even less rationally than children normally do. Keep in mind that while it's not normally enforced with much, high Rage Garou are off-putting to everyone; including post-Change Garou and even spirits. Children tend not to have a lot of Willpower compared to adults to keep their emotions in check.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I addition to genetics, there is a &quot;spiritual component&quot; to Garou. When does this spiritual change come about? At conception? At birth? At puberty? At the moment of first change? Pre-ordained by Gaia since the dawn of time? </div> </div> </div>There is no true genetic component in a scientific sense. Garou (and other shifters) might have patterns that can be studied and understood, but they don't follow human genetic science. The spiritual component is the primary component.<br /> <br /> The books rather purposefully avoid the conception vs. birth debate specifically, but given the nature of the Crinos-born, the implication is basically conception (or at least during fetal development as much of a difference as that makes). Basically, there is no &quot;spiritual change,&quot; because a pre-Change Garou is always part spirit. Their ability to exercise this to meaningful effect though doesn't come about until their first change (which is usually around puberty, part of why this isn't really a great game for &quot;pre-Change kids&quot;).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Can said spiritual component be detected by supernatural powers? </div> </div> </div>In theory. AFAIK there is no power in any of the books that just senses the spiritual component of a Garou specifically. Scent of the True Form lets you tell a Garou from a human (or whatever else) but it does so holistically, not by sensing specific &quot;components&quot; of a being. I feel like you might be taking the word &quot;component&quot; a bit different from it's intentions. Garou are full beings that cannot be reduced so simply into individual parts. Their spirit side and their physical side are not divisible, every part of them contains both.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Can pre-first change garou purchase Gnosis or Gifts in the manner of Kinfolk? </div> </div> </div>There's nothing stopping this broadly, but it's mechanically discouraged and the spirits might not teach a pre-Change Garou or even a Cub Gifts that they would teach a kin because they judge them by different standards.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Does silver pain or cause aggravated damage to garou pre first change? </div> </div> </div>No for homids and lupus, yes for Crinos-born (the books do like to make their lives suck). Keep in mind that homid and lupus Garou in their birth forms can handle silver and don't take Agg from it in general.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Can a garou awaken as a mage pre first change? </div> </div> </div>No. The Garou's spiritual nature is incompatible with having an avatar that can awaken.<br /> <br /> Most of the other crossover stuff is never touch on. Again, most Garou change during or right after puberty, and they can in theory change early as well as later. Most people would just have them undergo their First Change in response to things like this (or would have changed in the years of study necessary to learn something like the Rite of Rebirth, you need the Rituals Knowledge equal or greater to the level of the Rite to learn it, not something most tweens are going to have had time to do).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So, we know from the flavor text that most Garou have their first change when they frenzy for the first time after being placed in a stressful situation. </div> </div> </div>The First Change is triggered by any number of potential events (though usually stress, keeping in mind that children process stress differently than adults). The change also causes their first Frenzy, not the other way around, thus the rules for entering Frenzy aren't relevant: it's automatic.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This actually came up in my game, the PCs violently kidnapped an adolescent black spiral dancer who had not yet undergone her first change, and I made a rage roll for her to see if she would frenzy and undergo her first change as the result of the stress (she did) and the players told me I was cheating because, by definition, if she hasn't had her first change yet, she has no rage score to roll. </div> </div> </div>They're right, but you're more right. NPCs undergoing their First Change is entirely ST fiat territory, you didn't even have to give them a chance of a roll and could have just said it happened because they chose poorly by using violence on a pre-Change Garou.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Could such kinfolk ever breed true? </div> </div> </div>It's possible even when the animal kin aren't compatible. The Rev. section on this used the Bastet and Garou as an example, because the human kin of all the shifters can reproduce with each other.<br /> <br /> Though keep in mind that some changers work differently. The Corax stand out particularly in this regard.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-14T17:41:51-07:00","id":1537372,"title":"","content":"I would like to add my personal interpretation on the crossover questions. It's important to understand they're educated guesses at best, based on the idea that the pre-change Garou is a Garou nonetheless.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Talakeal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1537346-garou-pre-first-change#post1537346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What happens if a vampire tries to embrace a garou before their first change?</div> </div> </div> </div>A Garou usually has to botch on a Gnosis roll to be Embraced, becoming a hybrid Abomination. Since Gnosis is defined by Breed, it isn't hard to just apply the same rule.<br /> <br /> If you want to make this easier on pre-change, you can have the Embrace occur with a simple failure, but I would avoid to let it happen as easy as a normal human.<br /> <br /> The resulting vampire probably won't ever undergo a first Change, though. The easiest way to represent them would be as a normal vampire, with the caveat that they have their birth form. Whatever rules you make for pre-changers, look at the Abomination to see which ones would carry over if you want more complexity.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Talakeal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1537346-garou-pre-first-change#post1537346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can a garou awaken as a mage pre first change? What is awakening is forced on them by Alchemy Six or Prime Nine?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bMetaphysically the nature of a Garou is already a form of Awakening, or at least is so suggested by the M20 core (and I think it was mentioned elsewhere since 2nd Edition) and in-universe by some Mages.<br /> <br /> Probably a pre-changer can't Awaken, just as a Garou can't, anything that would cause an Awakening would instead trigger the First Change.<br /> \u200b<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Talakeal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1537346-garou-pre-first-change#post1537346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200b<br /> Is there any way a changeling soul can be attached to a garou pre first change?</div> </div> </div> </div>No.<br /> <br /> Changelings come in one of three ways: by the Changeling Way, by soul snatching, or by true birth of a new fairy.<br /> <br /> The Changeling Way happens in the womb or at conception. Such a child would never be a Garou in the first place because they're already a fairy.<br /> <br /> Soul Snatching is what the Sidhe usually do, but it is what it is. They don't attach to a human soul, they send the original soul to Arcadia and keep the body. You can rule that this is either impossible or at least harder to do with a Garou soul, I'd probably say impossible, but even if it does happen the result is a fairy in the otherwise human body that once belonged to a Garou.<br /> <br /> Birthing true is just that. It isn't explained by rules, but is mentioned a few times in Changeling lore. If both parents are Changelings, there's a chance that the child will be a new fairy soul. But as far as we know such a child is indistinguishable from any other Changeling, just lacking memories from previous lifes, and definitely wouldn't be a Garou.<br /> <br /> All that said, both Changelings can be Kinfolk and Garou can be Kinain. Two Changelings can have a baby together and this baby be a Kinain Garou. In fact, the chance is roughly the same of a Garou birth from non-fairy parents.<br /> \u200b<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Talakeal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1537346-garou-pre-first-change#post1537346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200b<br /> What would happen if a group pre first change performed the Rite of Sacred Rebirth?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bThe rite would probably fail, but leave a heavy Wyrm Taint.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Talakeal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1537346-garou-pre-first-change#post1537346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200b<br /> Or, even crazier, what would happen if a pre first change shapeshifter who was kin to multiple breeds performed the Rite of Sacred Rebirth to transform into a different breed than they would have become naturally with their first change?</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably the rite would fail, though exceptions might occur. If the ritual succeeds, then probably they would feel the loss of the Wolf or some other spiritual scar from losing their original breed, becoming effective Kinfolk.<br /> <br /> But since there's no version of the ritual for the other Fera, the very process of developing such a new ritual could result in something with stranger effects.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-14T22:57:39-07:00","id":1537381,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1537346-garou-pre-first-change?p=1537372#post1537372\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But since there's no version of the ritual for the other Fera, the very process of developing such a new ritual could result in something with stranger effects.</div> </div> </div> </div>It was a late addition, but there was a jaguar warrior ritual in Shattered Dreams, page 111. It doesn't change many specifics from the Garou version, save that it turns kinfolk into tainted Balam instead of tainted Garou.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-15T18:06:00-07:00","id":1537445,"title":"","content":"All of this is correct, except for two caveats.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1537346-garou-pre-first-change?p=1537356#post1537356\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In theory. AFAIK there is no power in any of the books that just senses the spiritual component of a Garou specifically. Scent of the True Form lets you tell a Garou from a human (or whatever else) but it does so holistically, not by sensing specific &quot;components&quot; of a being. I feel like you might be taking the word &quot;component&quot; a bit different from it's intentions. Garou are full beings that cannot be reduced so simply into individual parts. Their spirit side and their physical side are not divisible, every part of them contains both.</div> </div> </div> </div>As with the editions note above. This was true for 1st and 2nd edition. In Revised and W20 the pre-change Garou are not distinguishable from Kinfolk. Which makes for a much more interesting dynamic between kinfolk and Garou.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1537346-garou-pre-first-change?p=1537356#post1537356\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The First Change is triggered by any number of potential events (though usually stress, keeping in mind that children process stress differently than adults). The change also causes their first Frenzy, not the other way around, thus the rules for entering Frenzy aren't relevant: it's automatic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not all First Changes usually result in the first Frenzy. For some it can be a relatively straightforward process, especially for crinos-born who can just smooth into a form they need or when they yearn for something forbidden to them by their sheltered upbringing.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-16T01:27:52-07:00","id":1537471,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1537346-garou-pre-first-change?p=1537445#post1537445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As with the editions note above. This was true for 1st and 2nd edition. In Revised and W20 the pre-change Garou are not distinguishable from Kinfolk. Which makes for a much more interesting dynamic between kinfolk and Garou.</div> </div> </div> </div>W20 is the only edition that changed Scent of the True Form's wording to make Kin and Garou indistinguishable; and even then it only applies to that one Gift. Other methods (of which there are many in Rev. that W20 never says don't work, and due to W20's not create editing when it came to copying old material, it's implied at least a few still do).<br /> <br /> W20 certainly wants to created a different dynamic, but it never really committed to it beyond making it go from &quot;a level 1 Philodox Gift can tell the difference,&quot; to, &quot;the proper Rites or Talens can tell the difference,&quot; and acted like this would radically change anything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-16T02:02:23-07:00","id":1537474,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1537346-garou-pre-first-change?p=1537471#post1537471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> W20 is the only edition that changed Scent of the True Form's wording to make Kin and Garou indistinguishable; and even then it only applies to that one Gift. Other methods (of which there are many in Rev. that W20 never says don't work, and due to W20's not create editing when it came to copying old material, it's implied at least a few still do).<br /> <br /> W20 certainly wants to created a different dynamic, but it never really committed to it beyond making it go from &quot;a level 1 Philodox Gift can tell the difference,&quot; to, &quot;the proper Rites or Talens can tell the difference,&quot; and acted like this would radically change anything.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, this is one of those things where I've been sure that there was a difference between 2nd and Revised and that it came up at our table. We've been running it like that for a long time. I've just gone through the Revised books quickly and the only supporting evidence I can find for this is a part that says:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Moreover, it's not always possible to tell which children will Change and which won't. Certaing Gifts might offer a clue, but these are not used lightly. </div> </div> </div>- Player's Guide to the Garou pp. 55<br /> <br /> It's possible that it was just muddled there, but that Scent of True Form was supposed to work. The rest is just our table stuff it seems.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-16T06:30:10-07:00","id":1537482,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the replies!<br /> <br /> To respond to some specific comments:<br /> <br /> Any edition works. We wee actually mechanically playing nWoD Innocents in a setting that was based off cWoD werewolf twenty years after the events of The Last Battleground scenario destroyed the garou nation.<br /> <br /> The rite of Sacred Rebirth was, iirc, originally invented by the balam, so I assumed it would work for other changing breeds if it worked for garou.<br /> <br /> Sure, a human can be kin to multiple shifters (although i have heard people disagree and call the example in the Sam Haight story whose name i cant recall being non-canon), but afaik only Coyote and Wolves can produce fertile offspring in their animal form.<br /> So, our hypothetical coyote garou; would his lupus form be a coyote or a wolf? Would his crinos form resemble a coyote man or a more traditional werewolf?<br /> <br /> <br /> So the specific details of my game:<br /> <br /> The players are children who are, unknown to them, kinfolk. Some of them may become garou or other supernaturals later, but at the start they are mundane human kinfolk. <br /> One of the children became a Pooka.<br /> One of the NPCs was a changeling, but also a bsd kinfolk with gnosis, thus unable to undergo chrysalis following the rules in Unsung Heroes.<br /> The pooka PC used kenning on her, misunderstood what I said, and took it to mean she was both a Garou and a changeling.<br /> I decided to run with it rather than correct him, as I thought it was an interesting, if not technically legal idea to nave a garou soul and a changeling soul fighting lver the same body.<br /> The players decided to try and subdue her wolf side by having her wear enough silver to reduce her gnosis to zero, and then perform the rite of enchanting to awaken her fey side. Again, not technically legal, but I decided to let it work.<br /> The problem was, they decided to use force rather than trickery or diplomacy. I warned them that this could backfire, but they ignored me.<br /> I gave her a rage roll using the rage score she would have as a garou, and sure enough, she frenzied and underwent her first change.<br /> The players then started bitching and whining about how I had said she was physically abused by her BSD family, and if she hadn\u2019t undergo e the first change then, I was arbitrarily screwing them over by having her frenzy now. I said it wasn\u2019t arbitrary, it was up to the dice, and the players said that since pups dont have a rage score until their first change, making such a ruling was still screwing them over through storyteller fiat.<br /> I was then informed on another forum that the while situation was impossible in the first place because a pre first change garou can never have gnosis, and since the werewolf soul comes in at birth and detectable by gifts, there is no possibility of having a pup who doesn\u2019t know they are a garou rather than an ordinary kinfolk.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26576-talakeal","name":"Talakeal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-16T09:59:01-07:00","id":1537500,"title":"","content":"If the coyote Garou is the pup of a wolf and a coyote, even if the wolf is a Garou, the child's lupus form would be a coyote/wolf hybrid, and their Crinos too, although that would have no mechanical implication.<br /> <br /> Some people have this idea that it's impossible for a Garou to not know they're Garou, but that's simply bullshit. There's a lot of potential Garou around the world, testing every child is impractical, not to say impossible. As much as there are methods to find out, a lot of Garou go unnoticed until they change.<br /> <br /> Now, what you need is to have a honest conversation with your players, not to try to rules-lawyer your way out of this predicament. You gave in time and again to their antics until you didn't anymore, rules have nothing to do with that.<br /> <br /> You're the ST. You decide how things work. But they also have a right to know when rules aren't being strictly applied. Both sides erred here, though only you and your group can say how much.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-16T16:18:17-07:00","id":1537530,"title":"","content":"The whole coyote/wolf thing is probably not worth getting into too deeply. If you want something that more accurately reflects real world biology... you need to redo a lot of things. Otherwise you just need to use the reliable handwave of &quot;spirit magic&quot; and go with it.<br /> <br /> Most wolves and most coyotes in the Americas are hybrids as it is. Eastern grey wolves and red wolves are basically just long standing independent populations of hybrids.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-16T11:11:39-07:00","id":1538663,"title":"","content":"I have a couple of related questions:<br /> <br /> Does anyone know if there is a splat book that gives the exact gnosis loss for various items? I seem to recall it existing, but I can't find anything but the three items listed in the core book.<br /> <br /> Also, by the letter of the rules, each silver object made of or containing gives a full point of gnosis loss (except bullets for some reason), with no limits on weight. Do you actually play this way? Like, do you penalize players for old coins, or cell phones, or wedding rings for the silver within? If someone's Klaive breaks in half, does the gnosis loss suddenly double?<br /> <br /> Also, does anyone have any idea what the heck the WW20 book is on about with its &quot;80% pure jewelry silver&quot; claim? AFAICT such a thing doesn't exist in real life and most silver jewelry is either 92.5% sterling or .999% fine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26576-talakeal","name":"Talakeal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-16T12:20:51-07:00","id":1538668,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Talakeal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1537346-garou-pre-first-change?p=1538663#post1538663\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have a couple of related questions:<br /> <br /> Does anyone know if there is a splat book that gives the exact gnosis loss for various items? I seem to recall it existing, but I can't find anything but the three items listed in the core book.</div> </div> </div> </div>You'll find that in the core book of whichever edition you use. For W20, it's 259. Also, that'd be a weird thing to put in a tribe book, and even weirder to put in one for clans, traditions, etc.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, by the letter of the rules, each silver object made of or containing gives a full point of gnosis loss (except bullets for some reason), with no limits on weight. Do you actually play this way? Like, do you penalize players for old coins, or cell phones, or wedding rings for the silver within? If someone's Klaive breaks in half, does the gnosis loss suddenly double? </div> </div> </div>Bullets are a group affair, so if you have a bunch of smaller objects, you can handle it like that. If a klaive breaks into two equal pieces, it might be large enough to justify that, but in general, it's probably going with the larger piece or going by the bullet principle.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, does anyone have any idea what the heck the WW20 book is on about with its &quot;80% pure jewelry silver&quot; claim? AFAICT such a thing doesn't exist in real life and most silver jewelry is either 92.5% sterling or .999% fine. </div> </div> </div>You can also find it referred to as 800 or .800 silver.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-25T14:13:50-07:00","id":1539246,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Talakeal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1537346-garou-pre-first-change?p=1538663#post1538663\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have a couple of related questions:<br /> <br /> Does anyone know if there is a splat book that gives the exact gnosis loss for various items? I seem to recall it existing, but I can't find anything but the three items listed in the core book.<br /> <br /> Also, by the letter of the rules, each silver object made of or containing gives a full point of gnosis loss (except bullets for some reason), with no limits on weight. Do you actually play this way? Like, do you penalize players for old coins, or cell phones, or wedding rings for the silver within? If someone's Klaive breaks in half, does the gnosis loss suddenly double?<br /> <br /> Also, does anyone have any idea what the heck the WW20 book is on about with its &quot;80% pure jewelry silver&quot; claim? AFAICT such a thing doesn't exist in real life and most silver jewelry is either 92.5% sterling or .999% fine.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is interesting to me, like if your Homid Garou character goes to the 7-11 and buys a can of King, and the teller accidentally gives him a 1964 quarter as part of the change, he's in base form so the coin wouldn't do him damage, but would he be able to feel the coin is silver if it touched him? Or sense it without a gift with a successful primal urge even if it didn't touch him?<br /> <br /> Let's say other coins buffer it so it never touches his skin and he doesn't reflexively notice it with a Gift or a Sensing roll, what does the gnosis loss *feel* like? Like, obviously the ST tells the player, &quot;btw you're operating at one less gnosis than usual&quot; sometime before it becomes relevant, but what does the character experience, do they even know anything is wrong before they try to reach for or call upon their spiritual-understanding/(gnosis)? Maybe it feels like high tension power line buzzing, easy to tune out or even miss until you're trying to concentrate? But then again, you're moving a 'permanent' point on a character sheet up or down, it seems like it should feel dramatic.<br /> <br /> [edit]<br /> Would you allow that character a Sensing or Intelligence+Awareness/Primal Urge type roll to realize that it is the thing in his pocket doing this? I tend towards yes, but also 'hiding' silver amongst a Garou's possessions seems like a reasonable WtA plot point so I might not allow detection to be easy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27296,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27296-devidramoth","user":"Devidramoth","date":". 07-25-2024, 05:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27296-devidramoth","name":"Devidramoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27296_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-26T11:06:59-07:00","id":1539331,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1537346-garou-pre-first-change?p=1538668#post1538668\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You'll find that in the core book of whichever edition you use. For W20, it's 259. Also, that'd be a weird thing to put in a tribe book, and even weirder to put in one for clans, traditions, etc.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Bullets are a group affair, so if you have a bunch of smaller objects, you can handle it like that. If a klaive breaks into two equal pieces, it might be large enough to justify that, but in general, it's probably going with the larger piece or going by the bullet principle.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> You can also find it referred to as 800 or .800 silver.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, not a tribe book. I thought maybe in a Player's / Storyteller's guide or a book that had an expanded equipment / fetish / weapon list maybe.<br /> <br /> The set idea is odd to me, but could work. So like, a single coin or a bag of coins? Or like, silver earrings are 1 gnosis loss per 2, but silver rings are 1 to 1? What if your 5 bullets are mismatched from different guns?<br /> <br /> Than you for the info about .800 silver. That clears it up. It's so odd that they refer to it in the book with the confusing misnomer &quot;Jewelry Silver&quot; rather than a more common name like Continental Silver.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26576-talakeal","name":"Talakeal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-26T11:32:59-07:00","id":1539333,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Talakeal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1537346-garou-pre-first-change?p=1539331#post1539331\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, not a tribe book. I thought maybe in a Player's / Storyteller's guide or a book that had an expanded equipment / fetish / weapon list maybe.</div> </div> </div> </div>Those aren't splat books. A splat book involves an axis of character type - for W:tA, these are tribebooks, and potentially could have included auspices and breeds, but also includes the books on Fera. This is what you are referring to when you say a &quot;splat&quot;.<br /> <br /> If you're looking for an overall rules expansion, those are sourcebooks in the old tongue of the 90s. If you want a long list of fetishes, that'd be in Hammer and Klaive for Revised. You don't really find a general equipment guide, though; that information is scattered in a lot of places, like Book of the Weaver for technological items (&quot;Devices&quot;).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The set idea is odd to me, but could work. So like, a single coin or a bag of coins? Or like, silver earrings are 1 gnosis loss per 2, but silver rings are 1 to 1? What if your 5 bullets are mismatched from different guns? </div> </div> </div>Small items in general. And unless the bullet is mismatched to like, a cannon, it wouldn't probably make a difference.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Than you for the info about .800 silver. That clears it up. It's so odd that they refer to it in the book with the confusing misnomer &quot;Jewelry Silver&quot; rather than a more common name like Continental Silver. </div> </div> </div>It could have been a term familiar to the author of the section. English is not exactly standardized.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-05T19:37:00-07:00","id":1541626,"title":"","content":"Further question about silver and gnosis loss:<br /> <br /> Imagine you are a Werewolf Storyteller. One of the garou in your game carries a small silver token around for cosmetic / sentimental reasons.<br /> <br /> The token is something smaller than a single bullet and with no real use; say something like a coin, medallion, locket, ring, or wristwatch.<br /> <br /> Would you inflict a full point of gnosis loss on the character for doing so?<br /> <br /> I ruled that while the character would constantly feel the item as a minor irritant, I would not enforce such a harsh mechanical penalty on someone for no mechanical gain.<br /> <br /> I was then told that I was playing the game wrong, and allowing a garou to carry silver without mechanical penalty violates both the letter of the rules as well as the theme of the game. They went on to say that if I asked 100 experienced White Wolf players, all 100 of them would say that I was wrong to do so.<br /> <br /> <br /> So, while I doubt I will get 100 responses, I am curious to see how this shakes out. Thoughts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26576-talakeal","name":"Talakeal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-05T22:55:03-07:00","id":1541633,"title":"","content":"If your team and you had fun then it is game well played - there is not such thing &quot;playing the game wrong&quot;<br /> <br /> But it is true, for every object made of or containing silver that a werewolf is carrying, he loses one effective point from his Gnosis rating. More potent objects will cause the individual to lose more.<br /> Even a coin or medal, jewelry, etc can cause this especially if - and it is proboably the case if it is an important mememnto - he is &quot;attuned&quot; to it, so it will change with him, like cloths or such thing with a Rite - the spiritual connection is stronger and more become part of his self/spirit/soul etc. thus he feel &quot;more&quot; the burning of Luna's Metal<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","user":"Shadeprowler","date":". 09-06-2024, 02:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-05T23:19:30-07:00","id":1541635,"title":"","content":"While we old school WoD fans are a notoriously cantankerous bunch, I doubt you're going to find many people here that will agree that you were wrong even if we disagree in how we'd handle it.<br /> <br /> It is a violation of the rules of the game, I'd argue the case for it being a violation of the theme/spirit of the game is stronger than not, but the game has the &quot;Silver Rule&quot; in the book for a reason as well. TTRPG books aren't holy writ. If someone wants to run the game where a small mechanically useless silver trinket is insufficient to cause Gnosis loss, and the game is fun for their group? More power to you. The WoD games have always been written with the understanding that the fun of the group playing the game at their table is the right way to play the game for them; not what Internet forum debates on how to handle edge cases form as a consensus on what the most technically correct interpretation is.<br /> <br /> If you find 100 experienced White Wolf players that will agree on something unanimously it's the importance of being free to adjust the rules to your group's tastes; not how much silver is the minimum amount before you &quot;need&quot; to inflict the penalties the game sets out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-06T03:33:36-07:00","id":1541639,"title":"","content":"For whatever it's worth, I'd personally have the item inflict the penalty, but maybe ignore it in the larger picture if the PC had more silver with them.<br /> <br /> The very idea of this sentimental token would be all the more powerful if the player and character are whiling to pay the price.<br /> <br /> But then, there's no balance issues and no reason to step on your fun. Is the person that said those things a player in your game? If not, just politely ask them to mind their own business. This minor thematic issue isn't worth sweating over.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-07T11:48:41-07:00","id":1541692,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Talakeal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1537346-garou-pre-first-change?p=1541626#post1541626\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thoughts?</div> </div> </div> </div>You need to decide what the role of silver is in your chronicle setting. I rule that the Garou sensitivity to silver is a result of a ban from Luna. All gifts from spirits come with some sort of price or ban. Luna blessed the Changing Breeds to be able to change shape, but with it came vulnerability to silver because silver is the &quot;lunar metal&quot;, it symbolically represents the moon like gold does the sun.<br /> <br /> So I would lean that whenever the Garou carry silver, they have that penalty.<br /> <br /> I also understand the point a player is only doing something for flavor text reasons, and you don't want to punish the player for that. We also know that just having a fleck of silver doesn't produce results. If it is not at least 80% or 90% silver, it doesn't count. Many electronics contain some trace of silver. It might be less than a gram, but it is still there. But I don't think anyone would say a Garou shouldn't be able to hold a smartphone without a Gnosis loss, or lose Gnosis whenever they use a computer. Even the book says 1 point of lost Gnosis for 5 bullets, not 1 bullet (although that could also be read to mean that 1 Gnosis per 1-5 bullets, so you still lose at 1 bullet, but don't get 2 lost Gnosis until you reach 6). A klaive is obviously a big item. A small silver charm or jewelry is not.<br /> <br /> So I would be open to the idea that a single small piece of silver does not cause a loss of Gnosis (though if you have enough of them, it happens). Saying there is a sense of irritation would fit any thematic needs.<br /> <br /> So what's the limit before the Gnosis loss starts happening? I'd probably use 1 ounce so if the item contains less silver than that, there's no mechanical penalty. But just like it takes more than several bullets before it reaches the point of losing 2 Gnosis, not every silver object counts as another level of Gnosis loss. Use some commonsense.<br /> <br /> However, in all cases I would keep the idea that the mere touch of silver deals automatic aggravated damage per turn (unless in their breed form for homid or lupus). A silver ring, locket, coin, etc. can all directly touch the skin in ways that the trace silver in a cell phone does not because it is covered by lots of thing including its case. So that causes problems whenever the Garou does change regardless if the item is dedicated or not. If it is not dedicated, then the moment the Garou changes, she takes damage until presumably the item falls to the ground (and likely destroyed or damaged by the change). If it is dedicated (or because it is in something that is dedicated) so that it binds to the Garou's body, you're going to kill that character very quickly.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-09T11:55:57-07:00","id":1541790,"title":"","content":"@ Black Fox:<br /> <br /> That was almost word for word the same justification I used. People had ... strong opinions ... on it. Especially rejecting the notion that the amount of silver in the object had anything at all to do with it or that anyone could consider a cellphone as ever counting under any circumstances.<br /> <br /> <br /> I would say though that while I agree that jewelry will still be very painful outside of breed form (and if you change while wearing a silver ring, you are losing a finger!) I have a hard time justifying it doing damage that will be lethal after 21 seconds; even if it utterly annihilates the flesh it is in contact with, it still can't deal fatal wounds at that scale unless it contacts your heart / brain-stem.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26576-talakeal","name":"Talakeal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-09T13:19:52-07:00","id":1541796,"title":"","content":"If/when you do the damage thing, you just need to count it as a localized attack. Lets say a finger has 2 health levels for this purpose, so at 2 damage the finger is severed and no further damage occurs.<br /> <br /> And that's quite a specific situation anyways. The player will probably have at least one contingency to avoid this, depending on the actual object. We may very well be discussing rules for something that will never happen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-09T14:39:27-07:00","id":1541800,"title":"","content":"My solution to the whole technology issue (when it even comes up) is that the 80%+ silver content applies to any whole object, not just how much silver can be in an alloy and still count... which generally resolves Garou interacting with the small amounts of silver used for it's conductive properties in electronics. It also helps deal with the 80% or 90% lines in the books a bit if you are accounting for things like handle wraps counting against the total amount of non-silver allowed into a weapon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-10T14:17:41-07:00","id":1541886,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Talakeal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1537346-garou-pre-first-change?p=1541790#post1541790\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That was almost word for word the same justification I used. People had ... strong opinions ... on it. Especially rejecting the notion that the amount of silver in the object had anything at all to do with it or that anyone could consider a cellphone as ever counting under any circumstances.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sometimes you have to establish house rules based on your gaming group instead of what you think is correct as ST. If the consensus is strongly against you, sometimes it's better to concede. Or to ask the group to allow it for now, but revisit after a several game sessions and come to a group decision after seeing how it plays out. It all depends on how divisive and passionate your fellow gamers are. I've changed some of my decisions based on negative feedback. I've also been able to convince the group to give certain ideas or rulings a shot.<br /> <br /> Gaming is a social activity at its core so the &quot;correct&quot; answer is not always the best at each gaming table.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Talakeal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1537346-garou-pre-first-change?p=1541790#post1541790\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would say though that while I agree that jewelry will still be very painful outside of breed form (and if you change while wearing a silver ring, you are losing a finger!) I have a hard time justifying it doing damage that will be lethal after 21 seconds; even if it utterly annihilates the flesh it is in contact with, it still can't deal fatal wounds at that scale unless it contacts your heart / brain-stem.</div> </div> </div> </div>When talking about bans and the like, not everything makes sense from a purely material perspective. There's a spiritual component. Touching silver outside your breed form causes aggravated damage, period. It doesn't need to penetrate your skin and enter a vital organ. Instead, the presence of silver is more like fire, pollution, poison, or radioactivity than a knife or projectile wound. Arguing this radioactive piece of uranium isotype shouldn't kill you because it doesn't contact your heart or brain-stem doesn't make sense. It can kill just by being in your proximity, not even requiring touch. That's how I envision silver and its danger to Garou. If it makes physical contact with you outside of your breed form (meaning your natural form), you take damage.<br /> <br /> Of course, if you and your game group don't like that and have your own justification, you can always house rule it. But for my chronicles, if a Garou binds a silver item to them, it'll be a huge mistake. Of course, that should be well known so every Garou except the most ignorant will know to avoid that by the time of their Rite of Passage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-10T18:37:48-07:00","id":1541903,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1537346-garou-pre-first-change?p=1541800#post1541800\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My solution to the whole technology issue (when it even comes up) is that the 80%+ silver content applies to any whole object, not just how much silver can be in an alloy and still count... which generally resolves Garou interacting with the small amounts of silver used for it's conductive properties in electronics. It also helps deal with the 80% or 90% lines in the books a bit if you are accounting for things like handle wraps counting against the total amount of non-silver allowed into a weapon.</div> </div> </div> </div>IMO that creates more problems than it solves, as it makes it too easy to get around the core purpose of the ban; the disensentivise garou from carrying silver weapons to murder one another with. Many weapons have handles that are more than 20% of their mass, and most bullets have casings that are more than 20% of their mass, and if one could avoid the gnosis loss on a blade simply by attaching it to a very large hilt, well, I imagine klaives would have been replaced by silver tipped spears back in prehistory.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1537346-garou-pre-first-change?p=1541886#post1541886\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sometimes you have to establish house rules based on your gaming group instead of what you think is correct as ST. If the consensus is strongly against you, sometimes it's better to concede. Or to ask the group to allow it for now, but revisit after a several game sessions and come to a group decision after seeing how it plays out. It all depends on how divisive and passionate your fellow gamers are. I've changed some of my decisions based on negative feedback. I've also been able to convince the group to give certain ideas or rulings a shot.<br /> <br /> Gaming is a social activity at its core so the &quot;correct&quot; answer is not always the best at each gaming table.</div> </div> </div> </div>My players were fine with it actually, it was the people I was telling the story to who objected so strongly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26576-talakeal","name":"Talakeal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-10T19:10:31-07:00","id":1541908,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Talakeal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1537346-garou-pre-first-change?p=1541903#post1541903\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">IMO that creates more problems than it solves, as it makes it too easy to get around the core purpose of the ban; the disensentivise garou from carrying silver weapons to murder one another with. Many weapons have handles that are more than 20% of their mass, and most bullets have casings that are more than 20% of their mass, and if one could avoid the gnosis loss on a blade simply by attaching it to a very large hilt, well, I imagine klaives would have been replaced by silver tipped spears back in prehistory.</div> </div> </div> </div>If the total amount of silver drops too low, the object doesn't deal damage as silver as it is. A 70%/30% silver/steel blade is just a steel sword with an edge that doesn't last for both damage dealt and the Gnosis penalty.<br /> <br /> It's also quite in keeping with how the game present klaives as nearly all metal with minimal additions (usually nothing more than a leather wrap of the handle, or a handle made of other natural materials like bone, antler or wood, none of which weigh much).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-11T10:30:42-07:00","id":1541928,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1537346-garou-pre-first-change?p=1541908#post1541908\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If the total amount of silver drops too low, the object doesn't deal damage as silver as it is. A 70%/30% silver/steel blade is just a steel sword with an edge that doesn't last for both damage dealt and the Gnosis penalty.<br /> <br /> It's also quite in keeping with how the game present klaives as nearly all metal with minimal additions (usually nothing more than a leather wrap of the handle, or a handle made of other natural materials like bone, antler or wood, none of which weigh much).</div> </div> </div> </div>That seems an odd ruling to me; a spear with a silver tip or a car with a silver bumper should, imo, still do aggravated damage to garou, and the rules specifically say that a silver plated weapon works just fine until the plating gets worn away (iirc).<br /> <br /> But yeah, ymmw.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26576-talakeal","name":"Talakeal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-11T16:01:33-07:00","id":1541934,"title":"","content":"Plated silver working is optional, and if the ST allows it, is only supposed to work for one or two hits before the plating wears away too much to remain useful.<br /> <br /> Ultimately though, the game designers had a problem: they wanted silver to be &quot;special&quot; as a weakness (esp. to help maintain the spiritual aspects of the themes), but silver isn't that special as a material besides being valuable broadly. TTRPG players tend to be creative, and can come up with hundreds of ways to take advantage of the pop-culture weakness werewolves have to silver (which is also something pretty much everyone knows), which can be fun for a game about hunting werewolves, but becomes a serious problem for keeping things fun when you're playing the werewolves and you don't want a random human to TPK the party because you can just silver plate the bumper of a vehicle and plow into them.<br /> <br /> The only real solution is to limit what level of silver works. Hence you need to use relatively pure metallic silver in the rules, rather than anything with silver atoms in it being deadly to the Garou.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-11T16:09:40-07:00","id":1541936,"title":"","content":"The amount of damage done by Vehicular Homicide no Jutsu is so significant that having it be all agg just from a bumper (which might not even be the part that makes full contact with the character) is what seems odd. At least the plating on a weapon is over the entire weapon; the equivalent would be going through the trouble of coating the entire car in it, possibly even the windshield to some extent (though against Mokole, plating is, according to the breed book, ineffective, sloughing off immediately in the process of attack and never dealing agg at all, gold or silver).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-20T21:01:50-07:00","id":1542474,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Talakeal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1537346-garou-pre-first-change?p=1541626#post1541626\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thoughts?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not going to say a storyteller is wrong. It is important to make sure that the players know what world they are playing in, so it is important to make sure that the world elements don't come as a surprise to them or else they're going to have a hard time making sensible decisions as players. That being said, as long as you are being consistent and telegraphing your rulings, it makes sense to me that there are plenty of factors that are too small to be measured in a +/- 1 difficulty or +/- 1 die, so I'm not going to argue with the idea of a small irritating trinket not imposing a full penalty by itself. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27296-devidramoth","name":"Devidramoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27296_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}